From: Yimura <24669514+Yimura@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:39:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: add CRT screen-off animation

Add an opt-in CRT-style unlocked screen-off animation. CrtCollapseReveal
closes a mask vertically into a thin beam with a phosphor trail and
red/blue fringe, then contracts it to centre, ending on the scrim's end
colour. It draws masks over live content and captures no pixels.

LightRevealScrim gains a temporary screen-off override slot so base
wake and biometric effects keep updating underneath. The new
CrtScreenOffAnimationCoordinator samples Settings.Secure
lineage_screen_off_animation (0 Stock, 1 CRT; anything else or a read
failure falls back to Stock) once per accepted transition, installs and
clears the override, and exposes a dump plus a transition-only
LogBuffer. UnlockedScreenOffAnimationController keeps its stock gates,
500 ms reveal, 600 ms AOD delay and jank CUJs, and reports a typed
blocked reason.

Host tests were written but not executed: SystemUiRavenTests and
SystemUiRoboTests fail to compile on unrelated baseline fixtures
(FakeWifiRepository, FakeScreenRecordingService, BatteryRepositoryTest
and others); no CRT file reported an error. m SystemUI-core SystemUI
passes.

